WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.792
Here is a quick checkpoint.

00:00:01.792 --> 00:00:04.887
Which workflow is genuinely agentic?

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:09.107
Option one retrieves once and immediately generates.

00:00:09.107 --> 00:00:11.202
That is classic rag.

00:00:11.202 --> 00:00:19.702
Option two decides which source is needed, retrieves, grades the evidence, may retry or reroute, and then generates.

00:00:19.702 --> 00:00:27.032
That is agentic because the next action depends on the current state and observations.

00:00:27.032 --> 00:00:31.082
Option three simply uses a larger language model.

00:00:31.082 --> 00:00:34.655
Model size alone does not make the workflow agentic.

00:00:35.436 --> 00:00:38.068
The correct answer is the second workflow.

00:00:38.068 --> 00:00:41.238
The important idea is conditional control.

00:00:41.238 --> 00:00:45.596
The system can change what it does next based on what just happened.
